cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use dfo in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "dfo: a derivative-free optimization portfolio for bound-constrained black-box minimization"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Petrov
    given-names: Desislav
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-26"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dessvp/dfo"
url: "https://github.com/dessvp/dfo"
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  A portfolio for bound-constrained derivative-free minimization, written in
  Rust: Multilevel Coordinate Search, a quasi-Newton phase, lq-CMA-ES with
  BIPOP restarts, L-SHADE and a funnel race for multi-funnel landscapes. On
  the COCO/BBOB noiseless suite its score, averaged over budgets from 10·D to
  10^5·D evaluations, is higher than that of every archived dataset in each
  dimension from 2 to 40.
keywords:
  - derivative-free optimization
  - black-box optimization
  - CMA-ES
  - multilevel coordinate search
  - algorithm portfolio
  - COCO
  - BBOB
  - Rust
